    "id": "en_j2_vocab_065",
    "subject": "english",
    "grade": "junior2",
    "knowledge_tag": "词汇辨析",
    "ability_tag": "近义词辨析",
    "type": "multiple_choice",
    "question": "选择正确的单词填空。\n\n—Where is your father?\n—He _____ Shanghai on business.\n\nA. has been to\nB. has gone to\nC. went\nD. goes to",
    "options": [
      "A. has been to",
      "B. has gone to",
      "C. went",
      "D. goes to"
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "analysis": "【考点】have gone to（去了某地还没回来）。\n【解题思路】问「你爸爸在哪」，回答「他去了上海」，说明人在上海还没回来，用 has gone to。has been to 意为「去过（已回）」，went 是过去时（与现在无关）。\n【总结】经典考点：问「某人在哪」→ has gone to。问「某人是否去过某地」→ has been to。",
    "difficulty": 0.4
  },
  {
    "id": "en_j2_vocab_066",
    "subject": "english",
    "grade": "junior2",
    "knowledge_tag": "词汇辨析",
    "ability_tag": "近义词辨析",
    "type": "multiple_choice",
    "question": "选择正确的单词填空。\n\nThe two brothers look very _____. They are twins.\n\nA. same\nB. different\nC. similar\nD. like",
    "options": [
      "A. same",
      "B. different",
      "C. similar",
      "D. like"
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "analysis": "【考点】similar（相似的）vs same（相同的）vs like（像）。\n【解题思路】双胞胎长得像，用 similar（相似的）。same 前需要 the（look the same），like 是介词不是形容词（look like...）。\n【总结】look the same（看起来一样）/ look similar（看起来相似）/ look like + 名词（看起来像……）。",
    "difficulty": 0.4
  },
  {
    "id": "en_j2_vocab_067",
    "subject": "english",
    "grade": "junior2",
    "knowledge_tag": "词汇辨析",
    "ability_tag": "近义词辨析",
    "type": "multiple_choice",
    "question": "选择正确的单词填空。\n\nPlease speak _____. I can't hear you clearly.\n\nA. loud\nB. loudly\nC. aloud\nD. louder",
    "options": [
      "A. loud",
      "B. loudly",
      "C. aloud",
      "D. louder"
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "analysis": "【考点】loud vs loudly vs aloud 的区别。\n【解题思路】修饰动词 speak 用副词 loudly（大声地）。loud 也可作副词但多用于 talk/shout 后面（speak loud 较少用），aloud 意为「出声地」（区别于默读）。\n【总结】loud（形容词+副词，指声音大）/ loudly（副词，修饰动词）/ aloud（副词，出声地，如 read aloud 读出声）。",
    "difficulty": 0.5
  },
  {
    "id": "en_j2_vocab_068",
    "subject": "english",
    "grade": "junior2",
    "knowledge_tag": "词汇辨析",
    "ability_tag": "近义词辨析",
    "type": "multiple_choice",
    "question": "选择正确的单词填空。\n\nHe didn't go to bed _____ he finished his homework.\n\nA. if\nB. until\nC. when\nD. because",
    "options": [
      "A. if",
      "B. until",
      "C. when",
      "D. because"
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "analysis": "【考点】not...until...（直到……才……）。\n【解题思路】「直到做完作业才去睡觉」，用 not...until...。if 意为「如果」，when 意为「当……时」，because 意为「因为」。\n【总结】not...until... 是八年级高频考点：I didn't leave until the rain stopped.（雨停了我才离开。）",
    "difficulty": 0.4
  },
  {
    "id": "en_j2_vocab_069",
    "subject": "english",
    "grade": "junior2",
    "knowledge_tag": "词汇辨析",
    "ability_tag": "近义词辨析",
    "type": "multiple_choice",
    "question": "选择正确的单词填空。\n\nShe _____ her bag everywhere but couldn't find it.\n\nA. looked for\nB. found\nC. looked at\nD. looked after",
    "options": [
      "A. looked for",
      "B. found",
      "C. looked at",
      "D. looked after"
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "analysis": "【考点】look for（寻找）vs find（找到）。\n【解题思路】「到处找但没找到」用 look for（寻找的过程）。found 意为「找到了」与 couldn't find 矛盾。\n【总结】look for（寻找过程）/ find（找到结果）/ look at（看）/ look after（照顾）/ look up（查阅）/ look like（看起来像）。",
    "difficulty": 0.3
  },
  {
    "id": "en_j2_vocab_070",
    "subject": "english",
    "grade": "junior2",
    "knowledge_tag": "词汇辨析",
    "ability_tag": "近义词辨析",
    "type": "multiple_choice",
    "question": "选择正确的单词填空。\n\nHe _____ his bike, so he had to walk to school.\n\nA. lost\nB. missed\nC. forgot\nD. left",
    "options": [
      "A. lost",
      "B. missed",
      "C. forgot",
      "D. left"
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "analysis": "【考点】lose（丢失）vs miss（错过/想念）vs forget（忘记）vs leave（留下）。\n【解题思路】「只能走路去学校」暗示自行车丢了，用 lost。missed（错过），forgot（忘记）语义不符。\n【总结】lose 意为「丢失」，其过去式/过去分词是 lost。lose/lost/loss 是一组词：lose（动词）→ lost（过去式/形容词）→ loss（名词）。",
    "difficulty": 0.3
  },
  {
    "id": "en_j2_vocab_071",
    "subject": "english",
    "grade": "junior2",
    "knowledge_tag": "语境选词",
    "ability_tag": "词汇运用",
    "type": "multiple_choice",
    "question": "选择正确的单词填空。\n\nI can _____ hear what you're saying. Please speak louder.\n\nA. hard\nB. hardly\nC. harder\nD. hardest",
    "options": [
      "A. hard",
      "B. hardly",
      "C. harder",
      "D. hardest"
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "analysis": "【考点】hardly（几乎不）≠ hard（努力地/困难的）。\n【解题思路】「请大声点」暗示听不清，用 hardly（几乎不）表示否定含义。\n【总结】hard 既是形容词（困难的）也是副词（努力地），但 hardly 意思完全不同——「几乎不」，相当于 almost not。",
    "difficulty": 0.4
  },
  {
    "id": "en_j2_vocab_072",
    "subject": "english",
    "grade": "junior2",
    "knowledge_tag": "语境选词",
    "ability_tag": "词汇运用",
    "type": "multiple_choice",
    "question": "选择正确的单词填空。\n\nHe _____ his wallet at home this morning.\n\nA. forgot\nB. left\nC. put\nD. took",
    "options": [
      "A. forgot",
      "B. left",
      "C. put",
      "D. took"
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "analysis": "【考点】leave sth. at + 地点（把某物落在某处）。\n【解题思路】leave sth. + 地点 表示「把某物落在/忘在某处」。forgot 不能接具体地点（不说 forgot wallet at home）。\n【总结】经典易错点：leave sth. somewhere（正确）/ forget sth. somewhere（错误，应说 leave sth. somewhere 或 forget to bring sth.）。",
    "difficulty": 0.4
  },
  {
    "id": "en_j2_vocab_073",
    "subject": "english",
    "grade": "junior2",
    "knowledge_tag": "语境选词",
    "ability_tag": "词汇运用",
    "type": "multiple_choice",
    "question": "选择正确的单词填空。\n\n—Would you mind _____ the window?\n—_____. It's too hot in here.\n\nA. opening; Of course\nB. to open; Of course not\nC. opening; Of course not\nD. to open; Certainly",
    "options": [
      "A. opening; Of course",
      "B. to open; Of course not",
      "C. opening; Of course not",
      "D. to open; Certainly"
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "analysis": "【考点】Would you mind doing sth.?（你介意做某事吗？）\n【解题思路】mind 后接动名词 doing。回答「不介意」用 Of course not / Not at all / Certainly not。「Of course」等于「当然介意」，与语境矛盾。\n【总结】Would you mind doing...? 回答应注意：不介意 = 同意。Of course not = Not at all = Certainly not = No, not at all. 千万不要答 Of course（那等于介意）。",
    "difficulty": 0.5
  },
  {
    "id": "en_j2_vocab_074",
    "subject": "english",
    "grade": "junior2",
    "knowledge_tag": "语境选词",
    "ability_tag": "词汇运用",
    "type": "multiple_choice",
    "question": "选择正确的单词填空。\n\n_____ great fun it is to swim in summer!\n\nA. What\nB. What a\nC. How\nD. How a",
    "options": [
      "A. What",
      "B. What a",
      "C. How",
      "D. How a"
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "analysis": "【考点】感叹句：How + adj./adv. + 主语 + 谓语!\n【解题思路】fun 是不可数名词但也是形容词，此处 great fun 是形容词短语作表语，感叹部分是 great，所以用 How。What + (a/an) + adj. + n.，但 fun 在此作形容词用。\n【总结】感叹句判断方法：去掉修饰语看主语前面的词性。形容词用 How，名词用 What。It is great fun. → How great!",
    "difficulty": 0.5
  },
  {
    "id": "en_j2_vocab_075",
    "subject": "english",
    "grade": "junior2",
    "knowledge_tag": "语境选词",
    "ability_tag": "词汇运用",
    "type": "multiple_choice",
    "question": "选择正确的单词填空。\n\nHe stopped _____ and went on working.\n\nA. to smoke\nB. smoking\nC. smoke\nD. smoked",
    "options": [
      "A. to smoke",
      "B. smoking",
      "C. smoke",
      "D. smoked"
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "analysis": "【考点】stop doing sth.（停止做某事）vs stop to do sth.（停下来去做另一件事）。\n【解题思路】「停止（正在做的）然后继续工作」，用 stop doing sth.。stop to do 意为「停下来去做某事」。\n【总结】stop doing（停止正在做的事）/ stop to do（停下手头的事去做另一件事）。He stopped talking.（他停止说话。）He stopped to talk.（他停下来开始说话。）",
    "difficulty": 0.5
  },
  {
    "id": "en_j2_vocab_076",
    "subject": "english",
